1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,620
Marcus!

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:05,380
- What is it, Mother?

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,140
Where is your sister?

4
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:10,480
In the garden.

5
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:13,240
She is reading a book

6
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:15,880
under the old tree.

7
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:18,400
Call her, please.

8
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,640
Julia! Mother is calling you!

9
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:24,460
- I'm coming! - Hurry!

10
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:27,340
Julia, go to the market

11
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,220
and buy bread and milk.

12
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:32,080
Alone?

13
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,900
No, with your brother.

14
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:38,140
Marcus will carry the basket.

15
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:41,440
Marcus, do you have the money?

16
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:43,960
- Yes, in my bag.

17
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:46,780
Which road is shorter?

18
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:49,660
This one, by the river.

19
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:52,120
Look! A big dog!

20
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:54,580
Don't be afraid.

21
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:57,640
He is old and very gentle.

22
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:00,100
Whose dog is it?

23
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,380
The farmer's.

24
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:05,320
He lives near the bridge

25
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:08,560
with his wife and three sons.

26
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:11,200
This is the boy who

27
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:14,140
found our dog last year.

28
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:16,480
Hello, farmer!

29
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:20,320
- Hello, children! Where are you going?

30
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:22,660
To the market.

31
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,700
And then?

32
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,280
Home, before dark.

33
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:31,060
Good morning! I would like some bread.

34
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:33,520
How many loaves?

35
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:36,400
Two, and a little milk.

36
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:38,740
Anything else?

37
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:41,080
No, thank you.

38
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,600
Hey! Stop, thief!

39
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:45,940
He took my bag

40
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:48,820
and ran into the crowd.

41
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,920
Which way?

42
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:53,980
That way, past the temple!

43
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,200
Run, Marcus!

44
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:58,660
I can't see him.

45
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:01,540
There! Behind the cart.

46
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,520
Got him!

47
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:06,880
Give the bag back to my sister!

48
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:09,700
- Sorry! I was hungry.

49
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,520
Here, take this bread.

50
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:15,160
You are kind, girl.

51
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:18,580
Children, who wrote this letter?

52
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,440
Julia.

53
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:23,440
To whom did she write it?

54
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:26,080
To her grandmother.

55
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:28,960
And what did she write?

56
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:32,140
A short story about a horse.

57
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:34,900
Read it to us, Julia.

58
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,480
- Now? - Yes, now.

59
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:41,020
Once upon a time there was a horse

60
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:43,300
who could fly

61
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:46,660
over the mountains and the sea.

62
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:49,180
I don't know yet.

63
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:51,160
Why not?

64
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:54,460
Because I haven't finished it.

65
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:56,860
Your brother is

66
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:59,020
very brave.

67
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:02,080
When we reached the house,

68
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:04,600
the door was open

69
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,600
and the lamp was burning.

70
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:10,840
We waited for him in front of

71
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:13,180
the city gate.

72
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:15,940
If it rains tomorrow,

73
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,700
we will stay at home.

74
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,520
But if the sun shines,

75
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:24,340
we will go to the sea.

76
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,980
My father says that

77
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:30,280
the sea is too cold in spring.

78
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:33,940
I would swim if the water were warm.

79
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,220
- So would I.

80
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,620
Who is that man

81
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,140
in the red cloak?

82
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:43,600
The new teacher.

83
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,240
He came from Athens

84
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:48,400
last month.

85
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:52,060
♪ The moon is shining on the water ♪

86
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:55,660
♪ and the little boat is sleeping ♪

87
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:58,720
♪ Sleep, my child, sleep ♪

88
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:01,600
♪ until the sun rises ♪

89
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,360
Julia, are you tired?

90
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:06,940
- Yes, very tired.

91
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:09,400
And you, Marcus?

92
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:11,920
- I am not tired.

93
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:14,380
Dinner is ready.

94
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:16,540
What is it?

95
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:19,000
Fish with bread.

96
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,860
Oh no!

97
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:23,260
Don't complain,

98
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:26,200
or you will eat nothing.

99
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,780
Did you hear that?

100
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:30,700
- What?

101
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,580
A voice in the kitchen.

102
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:36,220
Maybe it's the cat.

103
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:38,920
We don't have a cat!

104
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:41,140
Wake Father.

105
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,600
Father! Wake up!

106
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:47,020
There is someone in the kitchen.

107
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,840
- Stay here, children.

108
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:52,120
Who is there?

109
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:54,400
It's only me,

110
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:57,880
your old friend from the village.

111
00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:01,180
Peter! What are you doing here

112
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,460
at this hour?

113
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:06,520
I lost my way in the dark.

114
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:08,920
Are you hungry?

115
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:11,080
- A little.

116
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:13,960
Julia, bring some bread

117
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,960
and the rest of the fish.

118
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:19,720
Stay with us tonight.

119
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:22,480
Good night, children!

120
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:25,720
♪ Sleep, my children, sleep ♪
